{%- comment -%}
  TJJM website overrides — one row per gym: ~Exact Gym Name|URL~
  Same idiom as tjjm-gym-addresses. Read by sections/tjjm-state-directory.liquid, which
  probes for '~' + name + '|' and takes everything up to the next '~'. An override WINS over
  the record's own "w" field, so this file can correct records in snippets/tjjm-gyms-data
  (the 113 KB legacy blob) without rewriting it.

  An EMPTY value blanks the link entirely — use it when a record carries a URL that provably
  belongs to a different business.

  RULES
  - The name must match EXACTLY, including punctuation and case.
  - Names must not contain '|' or '~'.
  - Only add a URL you have actually opened and confirmed is that location's page.
  - ONLY ADD AN ENTRY THAT CHANGES SOMETHING. Do not restate a URL the record already has:
    this file then becomes a second source of truth that silently pins the old value if the
    record is later corrected. Diff against the live data before adding.

  Created 5 Aug 2026 by the brand-cluster sister-site pass.

  WHY THESE ARE FEWER THAN THE CLUSTER SUGGESTED: the collision audit normalises URLs to
  DOMAINS, so tsk.com/locations/nj/hoboken/ and tsk.com/ both collapse to "tsk.com" and look
  identical. That made whole brands appear to point at their homepage when in fact only one
  or two records did. All 17 Tiger Schulmann's NJ records already had correct per-location
  URLs and need nothing here. Check raw "w" values, not normalised domains.
{%- endcomment -%}
